<title>UK: BADMINTON-WORLD RANKINGS.</title>
<headline>BADMINTON-WORLD RANKINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ardy B. Wiranata, winner of the</p>
<p>Indonesian Open at the weekend, jumps 10 places to ninth in the</p>
<p>world badminton rankings issued by the International Badminton</p>
<p>Federation on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Wiranata's win was his second of the season, the first being</p>
<p>a comeback victory at the Swedish Open is March.</p>
<p>At the top of the standings, Dong Jiong of China, who was</p>
<p>absent from the tournament in Solo, maintains a clear points</p>
<p>margin over his rivals.</p>
<p>In the women's rankings, Susi Susanti of Indonesia, also a</p>
<p>winner on Sunday, overhauls Gong Zhichao of China to move in to</p>
<p>second place behind China's Ye Zhaoying.</p>
<p>Leading rankings:</p>
<p>Men</p>
<p> 1. Dong Jiong  (China)		  308.60 points</p>
<p> 2. Park Sung-woo (South Korea)	270.21</p>
<p> 3. Sun Jun (China)			266.50</p>
<p>4. Poul-Erik Hoyer-Larsen (Denmark) 265.40</p>
<p> 5. Joko Suprianto (Indonesia)	 264.42</p>
<p> 6. Heryanto Arbi (Indonesia)	  262.67</p>
<p> 7. Peter Rasmussen (Denmark)	  257.91</p>
<p>8. Thomas Stuer-Lauridsen (Denmark) 233.36</p>
<p> 9. Ardy B. Wiranata (Indonesia)     224.40</p>
<p> 10.Budi Santoso (Indonesia)	   221.72</p>
<p>Women</p>
<p> 1. Ye Zhaoying  (China)		 361.06</p>
<p> 2. Susi Susanti (Indonesia)	   330.45</p>
<p> 3. Gong Zhichao (China)		 302.72</p>
<p> 4. Wang Chen  (China)		   277.22</p>
<p> 5. Camilla Martin (Denmark)	   269.92</p>
<p> 6. Mia Audina (Indonesia)	     267.58</p>
<p> 7. Zhang Ning  (China)		  251.40</p>
<p> 8. Dai Yun  (China)		     244.24</p>
<p> 9. Ra Kyung-min (South Korea)	 237.20</p>
<p> 10. Kim Ji-hyun (South Korea)	 229.78</p>
